LEARNER: Why does easing make it feel less robotic?
MENTOR: With linear keys, Title jumps straight to full speed at the first key and stops instantly at the last, and nothing physical moves like that, so it reads as a machine. Easing builds speed up gradually out of a key and lets it fade into the next, the way a real object speeds up and slows down, so the motion feels like it has weight.

